.TH ORG-TOOLS.TOML 5 "2026-11-13" "org-tools" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
org-tools.toml \- configuration file for the org command-line suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I .org-tools.toml
.br
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/org-tools/config.toml
.br
.I ~/.config/org-tools/config.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B .org-tools.toml
file configures formatting rules, lint diagnostics, Zettelkasten and authoring hygiene checks, agenda warning windows, workflow keywords, multi-vault
.B org-roam
directories, capture templates, and monorepo landscapes for
.BR org (1).
Configuration files use TOML syntax.
All settings are optional and fall back to Emacs Org-mode compatible defaults when omitted.
.SH CONFIGURATION HIERARCHY
.BR org (1)
resolves configuration settings from highest to lowest precedence:
.IP 1. 4
Explicit file path passed via the
.B \-\-config
command-line flag (skips global and ancestor discovery).
.IP 2. 4
Runtime environment variables such as
.B ORG_ROAM_DIRECTORIES
and
.BR ORG_TAG_COLUMN .
.IP 3. 4
Per-vault
.I <roam_dir>/.org-tools.toml
file when operating on a specific vault.
.IP 4. 4
Ancestor
.I .org-tools.toml
files discovered from the filesystem root down to the current working directory (plus
.I kb.toml
files up to the nearest
.I .git
root for landscape scope definitions).
.IP 5. 4
Global user configuration file specified by
.BR ORG_TOOLS_CONFIG ,
or
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/org-tools/config.toml
(falling back to
.IR ~/.config/org-tools/config.toml ).
.IP 6. 4
Built-in Emacs Org-mode compatible default values.
.PP
Path values expand
.IR ~/ ,
.IR $HOME/ ,
and
.I ${HOME}/
using
.B HOME
(or
.B USERPROFILE
on Windows), while relative paths resolve against the directory of the configuration file that declared them.
.SH SECTIONS
.SS [format]
Controls auto-fixable formatting rules (`F001` through `F005`):
.TP
.B trailing_whitespace \fR(boolean, default: \fBtrue\fR)
Remove trailing spaces and tabs from non-protected lines (`F001`).
.TP
.B blank_lines \fR(boolean, default: \fBfalse\fR)
Collapse consecutive blank lines to `max_consecutive_blank_lines` (`F002`).
.TP
.B max_consecutive_blank_lines \fR(integer, default: \fB1\fR)
Maximum consecutive blank lines permitted when `blank_lines` is enabled.
.TP
.B heading_blank_lines \fR(boolean, default: \fBfalse\fR)
Enforce blank lines before headings (`F003`).
.TP
.B heading_blank_lines_before \fR(integer, default: \fB1\fR)
Number of blank lines inserted before headings when `heading_blank_lines` is enabled.
.TP
.B table_format \fR(boolean, default: \fBtrue\fR)
Align Org pipe table columns and normalize separator rows (`F004`).
.TP
.B property_drawer_align \fR(boolean, default: \fBtrue\fR)
Align property values inside `:PROPERTIES:` drawers (`F005`).
.SS [lint], [lint.zettel], and [lint.authoring]
Controls structural, stylistic, and opt-in hygiene lint rules (`E001` through `I008`):
.TP
.B disabled_rules \fR(array of strings, default: \fB[]\fR)
Rule identifiers or kebab-case names to skip during `org fmt check` and `org lsp` (for example, `["W001", "heading-level-gap"]`).
.TP
.B enable \fR(array of strings, default: \fB[]\fR, alias: \fBenabled_rules\fR)
Opt-in rule identifiers or names to activate (`"W038"`, `"W039"`, `"I008"`).
.TP
.B id_scope \fR(string, default: \fB"vault"\fR)
Resolution boundary for duplicate `:ID:` checks (`E002`), `org-edna` `ids(...)` (`W036`), and cross-file links (`W037`): `"vault"`, `"roam-dir"`, `"dir"`, or `"file"`.
.TP
.B [lint.zettel] forbid_tasks \fR(boolean, default: \fBfalse\fR)
Enable `W038` (`zettel-task-hygiene`) forbidding active TODO keywords and checklists inside concept notes.
.TP
.B [lint.authoring] forbid_ephemeral_headers \fR(boolean, default: \fBfalse\fR)
Enable `W039` (`ephemeral-file-headers`) flagging `#+DATE:` and `#+AUTHOR:` file headers.
.TP
.B [lint.authoring] max_table_cell_chars \fR(integer, optional)
Enable `I008` (`oversized-table-cell`) when any non-separator table cell exceeds this character threshold (for example, `120`).
.SS [agenda]
Controls daily and weekly agenda timeline projection:
.TP
.B deadline_warning_days \fR(integer, default: \fB14\fR)
Lead-time warning window in days for `DEADLINE:` timestamps without an explicit `-Nd` warning suffix.
.SS [todo]
Defines fallback workspace-wide TODO state sequences when files omit `#+TODO:`, `#+SEQ_TODO:`, `#+TYP_TODO:`, or `#+SETUPFILE:`:
.TP
.B sequences \fR(array of strings, default: \fB[]\fR)
Additive Org workflow sequence specifications using `|` to separate active and completed states (for example, `["TODO(t) NEXT(n) WAITING(w) | DONE(d) CANCELLED(c)"]`).
.TP
.B keywords \fR(array of strings, default: \fB[]\fR)
Optional token list joined and parsed as a single sequence when `sequences` is empty.
.TP
.B todo \fR(array of strings, default: \fB[]\fR)
Explicit active ("not done") workflow keywords used when `sequences` and `keywords` are empty.
.TP
.B done \fR(array of strings, default: \fB[]\fR)
Explicit terminal ("done") workflow keywords paired with `todo`.
.SS [roam] and [roam.directories]
Configures multi-vault `org-roam` v2 directories, default subdirectories, capture editor, and daily logging:
.TP
.B [roam.directories] \fR(table or array of strings, default: \fB{}\fR)
Named vault map (`work = "~/org/work"`, `private = "~/org/private"`) or array (`directories = ["./work", "./private"]`). Overridable at runtime via `ORG_ROAM_DIRECTORIES`.
.TP
.B default_directory \fR(string, optional)
Default vault name or path used when `--roam-dir` is omitted.
.TP
.B gtd_subdir \fR(string, default: \fB"gtd"\fR)
Vault-relative subdirectory storing base GTD files (`inbox.org`, `gtd.org`, `projects.org`, `habits.org`, `calendar.org`) and `projects/`.
.TP
.B zettel_subdir \fR(string, default: \fB"zettel"\fR)
Vault-relative subdirectory storing permanent Zettelkasten concept notes.
.TP
.B fleeting_subdir \fR(string, default: \fB"fleeting"\fR)
Vault-relative subdirectory storing Luhmann fleeting thought notes.
.TP
.B daily_subdir \fR(string, default: \fB"daily"\fR)
Vault-relative subdirectory storing `YYYY-MM-DD.org` daily journal notes.
.TP
.B editor \fR(string, optional)
Editor command spawned for interactive captures (overrides `$VISUAL` and `$EDITOR`).
.TP
.B log_to_daily \fR(boolean, default: \fBfalse\fR)
Append a timestamped link under `* Captured today` in `daily/YYYY-MM-DD.org` during captures and transformations.
.SS [capture.templates.<name>]
Defines custom capture templates or overrides built-in templates (`zettel`, `concept`, `technical`, `howto`, `person`, `place`, `project`, `fleeting`, `daily`, `inbox`):
.TP
.B description \fR(string, optional)
Human-readable summary displayed by `org roam capture --list-templates`.
.TP
.B keys \fR(string, optional)
Short key selector usable with `org roam capture -t <key>`.
.TP
.B kind \fR(string, default: \fB"file"\fR)
Target granularity: `"file"` (level-0 `org-roam` file node) or `"entry"` (heading entry).
.TP
.B target \fR(string, default: \fB"<zettel_subdir>/${slug}.org"\fR)
Vault-relative destination path supporting `${...}` variable interpolation.
.TP
.B target_heading \fR(string, optional)
Parent heading title under which new entries are filed when `kind = "entry"` (for example, `"* Inbox"`).
.TP
.B roam_type \fR(string, optional)
Sets `:TYPE:` inside the node's `:PROPERTIES:` drawer.
.TP
.B properties \fR(table of strings, default: \fB{}\fR)
Additional `:PROPERTIES:` key-value pairs supporting `${...}` interpolation.
.TP
.B filetags \fR(array of strings, default: \fB[]\fR)
Filetags (when `kind = "file"`) or heading tags (when `kind = "entry"`).
.TP
.B todo_header \fR(string, optional)
Optional `#+TODO:` header line emitted when creating a new file.
.TP
.B head \fR(string, optional)
Optional extra preamble lines emitted when creating a new file.
.TP
.B body \fR(string, optional)
Inline Org body template supporting `${id}`, `${title}`, `${slug}`, `${date}`, `${timestamp}`, `${timestamp_inactive}`, `${timestamp_active}`, `${roam_dir}`, `${body}`, `${medium}`, `${location}`, `${parent}`, and custom `--var` placeholders.
.TP
.B body_file \fR(string, optional)
Path to an external `.org` body scaffold file used when `body` is omitted.
.TP
.B edit \fR(boolean, optional)
Default interactive editor launch behavior when `--edit` and `--no-edit` are omitted.
.SS [landscapes.<slug>] and [projects.<slug>]
Defines composable monorepo project clusters and forge patterns (also read from `kb.toml`):
.TP
.B [landscapes.<slug>] description \fR(string, optional)
Human-readable summary of the landscape scope.
.TP
.B [landscapes.<slug>] projects \fR(array of strings, default: \fB[]\fR)
Member project slugs belonging directly to `<slug>`.
.TP
.B [landscapes.<slug>] forges \fR(array of strings, default: \fB[]\fR)
Repository forge path or glob patterns belonging to `<slug>` (alias: `forge_prefixes`).
.TP
.B [landscapes.<slug>] includes \fR(array of strings, default: \fB[]\fR)
Slugs of child landscapes transitively included with cycle protection.
.TP
.B [projects.<slug>] description \fR(string, optional)
Human-readable summary of an individual project.
.TP
.B [projects.<slug>] forge \fR(string, optional)
Canonical repository forge path for `<slug>`.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .org-tools.toml
Project or vault configuration file.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/org-tools/config.toml
User-global fallback configuration file (`~/.config/org-tools/config.toml` when unset).
.SH EXAMPLES
Configure opinionated formatting, Zettelkasten hygiene, multi-vault directories, and an inbox template:
.PP
.nf
    [format]
    blank_lines = true
    heading_blank_lines = true

    [lint]
    enable = ["W038", "W039"]
    id_scope = "vault"

    [lint.zettel]
    forbid_tasks = true

    [agenda]
    deadline_warning_days = 10

    [todo]
    sequences = ["TODO NEXT WAITING | DONE CANCELLED"]

    [roam]
    default_directory = "work"
    log_to_daily = true

    [roam.directories]
    work = "~/org/work"
    private = "~/org/private"

    [capture.templates.inbox]
    description = "Quick inbox task"
    keys = "i"
    kind = "entry"
    target = "gtd/inbox.org"
    target_heading = "* Inbox"
    body = "${body}"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.B org(1)
